"""Generate analysis handoff tables from completed empirical result artifacts."""
import hashlib,json,pathlib
import numpy as np,pandas as pd
from benchsmall.metrics import paired_interval
root=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];out=root/'results/study'
macro=pd.read_csv(out/'macro_repeats.csv');contrast=pd.read_csv(out/'paired_contrasts.csv');robust=pd.read_csv(out/'robustness_macro.csv');formula=pd.read_csv(out/'aipw_formula_repeats.csv')
fm=[]
for k,g in formula[formula.scenario=='main'].groupby('budget'):
 for metric in ['mae_pp','rmse_pp','spearman','kendall_tau_b','bias_pp']:
  bydraw=g.groupby('repeat')['difference_'+metric].agg(['mean','count'])
  fm.append({'budget':int(k),'metric':metric,'direction':'code10 minus paper10','n_benchmarks_min':int(bydraw['count'].min()),'n_benchmarks_max':int(bydraw['count'].max()),**paired_interval(bydraw['mean'])})
pd.DataFrame(fm).to_csv(out/'aipw_formula_macro.csv',index=False)
def fmt(v):return f'{v:.4f}' if pd.notna(v) else 'undefined'
def markdown(df):
 text=['| '+' | '.join(map(str,df.columns))+' |','| '+' | '.join(['---']*len(df.columns))+' |']
 for row in df.itertuples(index=False,name=None):text.append('| '+' | '.join(fmt(v) if isinstance(v,(float,np.floating)) else str(v) for v in row)+' |')
 return '\n'.join(text)
means=macro.groupby(['budget','method'])[['mae_pp','rmse_pp','spearman','kendall_tau_b']].mean().reset_index()
cc=contrast[(contrast.benchmark=='MACRO13')&(contrast.method=='crossfit_difference')&(contrast.metric=='mae_pp')][['budget','reference','difference','ci_low','ci_high','bootstrap_low','bootstrap_high']]
rr=robust[(robust.metric=='mae_pp')&robust.method.isin(['random_mean','source_difference','ridge','aipw_paper','crossfit_difference','mirt_random_gp'])][['method','condition','n_benchmarks_min','difference','ci_low','ci_high']]
collisions=pd.read_csv(out/'response_collisions.csv');collisions=collisions[collisions.scenario=='main'].groupby('benchmark').agg(targets=('target_row','count'),patterns=('response_pattern','nunique'),source_matches=('source_match','sum')).reset_index()
text='''# Completed analysis evidence and interpretation

All quantities below are generated by `diagnostics/write_evidence_note.py` from the saved result files; error units are percentage points. This is the analysis owner's evidence handoff, not a manuscript or a novelty claim.

All13 benchmarks,3 main budgets,20 final draws,18 main methods,26 source-size and6 eligible proxy-family cases completed. The219 source fits (168 development+51 selected historical refits) all met the fixed relative-objective convergence criterion;13 used the declared continuation. This is optimizer success, not a certificate of global optimality or negligible gradient: the largest saved gradient component is1.249881. There are1,611,440 immutable target predictions in22,360 benchmark/scenario/budget/draw/method cells. Every access/cell check and independent truth/baseline/clipping/error check passed. Final metric tables have80,840 rows and10,605 paired contrasts.

The crossfit candidate improves macro score error over random means and fixed source-difference, but has larger MAE/RMSE than learned-score ridge at every studied budget. Against tuned paper-AIPW it has no resolved k10 MAE advantage and is worse at k30/k100 under the conditional intervals. The finite-population expectation identity does not establish predictive-risk or ranking superiority. These are finite-set observations; no universal method winner, future-model coverage or new residual-correction novelty follows.

## Main mean metrics

Equal-weight benchmark macro averages, first averaged within each paired draw. Undefined source-prior rank values are retained as undefined. Error values use raw predictions; only rank/tie comparisons use the documented12-decimal numerical convention. The full benchmark heterogeneity remains in `summary.csv` and `paired_contrasts.csv`; these means must not replace those outcomes.

'''+markdown(means)+'''

## Candidate-minus-reference macro MAE

Negative differences favor the candidate. Intervals are95% paired t intervals for the mean across20 independently sampled item orderings, conditional on the fixed historical/target pools. Bootstrap endpoints are5000 paired-draw percentile sensitivity checks. They are not coverage intervals for a future draw, target, family or benchmark population, and no multiplicity correction licenses a significance tally. Anchor fits/selections are fixed; copied repeats supply no fit uncertainty.

'''+markdown(cc)+'''

At matched candidate alpha, residual correction increases k10 MAE but reduces k30/k100 MAE relative to the same half-sample imputer. The separately tuned uncorrected aggregate is stronger than the candidate at all three budgets; that comparison additionally changes regularization. Full-fit ridge imputation is another stronger control, so a crossfit-versus-AIPW difference cannot be assigned solely to splitting or correction. Rank improvement is a separate question; source-difference and random mean must have identical within-draw ranks because one adds a common constant.

## Source-size and family-exclusion sensitivity at k30

Condition-minus-reference MAE, paired on exactly the same target cohort and item draws. Source25/50 means use13 benchmarks; the family-exclusion stress test uses6 eligible name-proxy cohorts, not verified lineage or a novel target population. ARC had no eligible family and HELM identity alignment was not inferred. These quantities summarize sensitivity, not independently sampled model populations.

'''+markdown(rr)+'''

## Retrospective response collisions

Complete-response hashes enter only after prediction. Distinct names/opaque HELM rows remain the primary population; `response_patterns`, source-match and no-match outputs in `metrics.*`/`summary.csv` expose alternative descriptive populations. Do not replace them with claims of collision-free or family-independent evaluation.

'''+markdown(collisions)+'''

## Matched-alpha AIPW formula effect

The primary tuned-paper/fixed-alpha10-code comparison combines formula and alpha. The separate table below isolates the same alpha10 fit using **paper10=(1-k/N)*code10+(k/N)*random_mean**. No extra observations, fitting or tuning enter. The direct disposable-estimator check agrees to1e-12. Per-target reconstruction and all per-benchmark paired effects are saved in `aipw_formula_predictions.parquet`, `aipw_formula_repeats.csv` and `aipw_formula_contrasts.csv`.

'''+markdown(pd.DataFrame(fm)[['budget','metric','difference','ci_low','ci_high','n_benchmarks_min']])+'''

## Numerical validity, chronology and failures

Raw exact-float rank processing fragmented mathematical ties. The initial outputs are preserved in `original_raw_ties/`. The post-scoring repair is explicitly dated in `notes/postscore_amendments/2026-11-05_rank_numerics.json`; it changes no predictions, fitting, tuning or target access. All80,840 error/bias/tail/out-of-range rows remain bitwise identical, all1,420 constant-shift rank/tie/inversion comparisons pass, and22,360 independent12-decimal rank calculations agree (`rank_correction_checks.json`). Precision10 differs from12 in one cell (maximum Spearman0.000141/tau-b0.000160); precision14 changes27 cells, with maximum Spearman0.098376 (6 source-difference cells,20 copied MuSR anchor cells from one fixed fit, and1 learned-imputer cell). The independently verified count-rank ties explain the first26; rounding does not prove that every nearly equal learned prediction is a mathematical tie. Twelve decimals is one fixed operational numerical tie convention, not a rule selected per method/dataset and not a universal translation-invariance theorem. Retain that sensitivity rather than asserting complete numerical identity. `rank_precision_macro_contrasts.csv` and `rank_precision_conclusion_sensitivity.csv` quantify the resulting primary macro contrast/endpoint changes. The1pp pair-gap boundary is canonicalized as part of this numerical fix. No ranking finding was used to refit/select methods.

Original v1 authorization, exact-hash v2 extension and target execution chronology are preserved in `config/gate.json`, `gate_followup.json` and `notes/execution_gate.md`. Formal amended-scorer-hash GO publication followed prediction launch; it is not backdated. The plan owner states no rerun is needed because predictor/tuning/data/split/item bytes are unchanged. Initial whole-matrix audit access is disclosed separately from the enforced predictor API budgets; this is a reproducible guard, not a cryptographic holdout. One supplemental formula-diagnostic job failed because a glob included timing parquet files; it was fixed and rerun with no primary result dropped (`notes/run_failures.json`). Numerical raw-rank repair and initially capped fits are not concealed.

## Compute and reproduction limits

The two cache-reusing prediction commands consumed67.467847 measured process CPU seconds in total (elapsed37.751993s and29.825421s, concurrent), with maximum process peak RSS473992KiB. Original scoring consumed234.204501 CPU seconds; corrected scoring consumed237.244579 CPU seconds, with the largest scoring process peak1252804KiB. These are measured command costs with loading/output overhead, excluding source fitting. There is no fabricated end-to-end source CPU total:219 fit records save elapsed time, and one spans world suspension. The218 unaffected fit components sum1312.549191s elapsed; the affected original remains165044.541180s inclusive of suspension. Its separate identical-source timing replication measured173.821535s elapsed/173.778573s CPU and is not a reconstruction of original active elapsed time. Cache sharing, per-method-alone anchor costs and reused mixture inference are explained in `notes/timing_caveat.md`; do not sum duplicated cost fields as executed work. Raw whole-command measurements and all diagnostic costs are retained in `results/study/execution/`.

CPU-only fitting is nonconvex MAP-MIRT with a single fixed initialization/penalty and disclosed adapters, not the published variational hierarchical implementation or all IRT methods. Historical pools can contain related model identities; HELM rows are opaque, family groups are name proxies, and constant/duplicate response vectors remain visible. k100 is up to22.88% of the smallest matrix, so it is not always a tiny subset. The minimum true-score grid step is not a minimum learned-prediction gap. A single fixed target pool per matrix, small HELM validation cohorts, one fixed anchor seed and conditional item-draw intervals constrain transfer claims. The finite20-draw variance/squared-mean-error decomposition is descriptive, not an estimator of population design bias.
'''
integrity=json.loads((out/'aipw_formula_integrity.json').read_text())
text+='\nThe same-alpha reconstruction also agrees with '+str(integrity['target_predictions_checked'])+' actual preselected-alpha10 primary target predictions across '+str(integrity['benchmark_scenario_budget_draw_cells_checked'])+' cells, maximum absolute discrepancy '+str(integrity['max_abs_direct_primary_alpha10_minus_reconstruction'])+' (`aipw_formula_integrity.json`).\n'
compute_path=out/'compute_accounting.json'
if compute_path.exists():
 compute=json.loads(compute_path.read_text())
 text+='\nSupplemental whole-command source timing replay completed and verified all'+str(compute['source_replay_fits_verified'])+' fits/'+str(compute['source_replay_tuning_cases_verified'])+' tuning cases against the preserved originals. It consumed'+f"{compute['source_replay_cpu_seconds']:.3f}"+' CPU seconds, with an observed two-job parallel wall span of'+f"{compute['source_replay_observed_parallel_wall_span_seconds']:.3f}"+'s. Source replay plus the original cached-prediction and corrected-scoring phases total'+f"{compute['reproduction_workload_cpu_seconds']:.3f}"+' CPU seconds as a reproduction-workload proxy, measured across separate runs. One GSM/main/k30 correctness-anchor ridge development loss grid differs (maximum0.4511713pp), with unchanged chosen alpha1; all45 selected-parameter packages and219 fits agree. All78 final anchor selections and their mean predictions reproduce exactly in `anchor_reproduction_audit.json`. A bounded1/2-thread diagnostic reproduces both loss grids exactly:1 thread matches the replay and2 threads match the original, with one of30 development representatives changed and alpha1 retained. This establishes numerical thread sensitivity; the original effective thread-pool count was not recorded, so historical execution settings are not inferred as fact. The replay is not labeled an exact reproduction of every intermediate. This does not recover original source CPU or original end-to-end wall time; pilots, acquisition, diagnostics and rendering are excluded. See `notes/compute_accounting.md` and `results/study/compute_accounting.json` for exact stage measurements/hashes. No original scientific evidence is replaced.\n'
(root/'notes/results_interpretation.md').write_text(text)
print('Generated analysis evidence note and fixed-alpha macro effects.',flush=True)
